  "dependency": "DUB-17 Theorem 2.6 / DUB-18 Corollary 8.2 -> literal higher symmetric-power continuation -> arithmetic automorphy -> original all-weight characteristic-zero association -> actual finite Gamma1 Hecke-character realization -> actual Picard/H1, full/parabolic, transpose/diamond comparison retaining the homogeneous coefficient endomorphism -> actual differential/cusp comparison -> arbitrary cusp differential realization -> original integral-ratio field membership -> bounded denominators for rational Fourier cusp forms.",
  "discharged": "For actual Gamma1 cusp forms with rational width-one Fourier coefficients and explicit balance k+4a+6b=12m, derive original cyclotomic Fricke membership and rational j-integrality. Actual Fricke generators supply bounded fractions. Normalize a nonzero denominator coefficient and take the native cyclotomic trace to obtain a nonzero rational bounded fraction. Native Laurent localization and normality, after finite integer scaling of the monic relation, give a uniform integer bound. The original E4/E6 integer units and integral discriminant cancel the auxiliary weight factors, giving one integer multiple of the original cusp form with a literal integer Fourier series. The already proved full-space rational Fourier spanning then gives integral Fourier spanning; for weight two a=b=m=1, at every nonzero level.",
  "boundary": "Scratch-audited only; promotion and assembled verification pending. Integral Fourier spanning is an inner obligation. Actual arbitrary Gamma1 cusp differential realization and its converse remain, followed by the original Picard/H1, full/parabolic, transpose and diamond comparison retaining the homogeneous coefficient endomorphism. Finite-character arithmetic realization, original all-weight characteristic-zero association, local/image/regularity, automorphy and literal higher symmetric-power continuation remain. No characteristic-zero lift is inferred from finite characters or deformation rings. All original twenty gates remain; 16/20; DUB-17--20 OPEN.",
